> Generated with the AI Coding Tool Validation Kit {{kit_version}}. This is a checklist template: copy it for each execution, record who did each check and when, and file the completed copy as a record. Approval of each completed execution is given in the eQMS.

## 1. Purpose and scope

AI coding tools spread faster than inventories are updated: IDE extensions, review bots, CI actions, cloud agents and personal accounts appear without a formal request. This checklist finds AI tools that are in use at {{org_name}} and reconciles them with the software inventory, so that every QMS-relevant tool is registered, validated or stopped. No shadow AI: a tool the organisation does not know about cannot be validated, controlled or defended in an audit.

When to run it:

- before the validation plan of a tool is approved (initial validation{{#already_in_use}}, and as part of the interim-use justification{{/already_in_use}});
- at every periodic review, every {{periodic_review_months}} months;
- when a trigger occurs: a new AI vendor invoice, a new GitHub / GitLab app or bot, a report under the work instruction {{doc_id_wi}}.

